msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BEETA.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BEETA.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"Beetas are insectoid creatures that enjoy a symbiotic relationship with the radioactive environment they thrive in.\n"
"\n"
"Much like the honey bee gathers nectar and processes it to honey, the Beeta turns <link=\"URANIUMORE\">Uranium Ore</link> into <link=\"ENRICHEDURANIUM\">Enriched Uranium</link> through a complex process of isotope separation inside the Beeta Hive.\n"
"\n"
"When first observing the Beeta's enrichment process, many scientists note with surprise just how much more efficient the cooperative combination of insect and hive is when compared to even the most advanced industrial processes."
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BEETA.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BEETA.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Aggressive Critter"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BEETA.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BEETA.TITLE"
msgid "Beeta"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.HEADER_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.HEADER_1"
msgid "Basic Needs"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.HEADER_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.HEADER_2"
msgid "Worker Optimization"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.PARAGRAPH_1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.PARAGRAPH_1"
msgid ""
"<link=\"POWER\">Power</link>: Bionic Duplicants run on portable <link=\"ELECTROBANK\">Power Banks</link> that they automatically replace during scheduled Downtime. If power banks are depleted, the Bionic Duplicant will become Powerless and may perish if they deplete their <link=\"OXYGEN\">Oxygen</link> tanks before being rebooted.\n"
"\n"
"<link=\"GUNKEMPTIER\">Gunk Extractors</link>: Bionic systems must dispose of built-up <link=\"LIQUIDGUNK\">Gunk</link> every {time}, or risk making a mess. If there are no purpose-built extractors available, Bionic Duplicants will clog a nearby <link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSTOILETTYPE\">Toilet</link>.\n"
"\n"
"<link=\"BUILDCATEGORYOXYGEN\">Oxygen</link>: Bionic Duplicants ventilate their mechanisms using internal <link=\"OXYGEN\">Oxygen</link> tanks. These must be refilled every {number} to prevent suffocation. They do not produce <link=\"CARBONDIOXIDE\">Carbon Dioxide</link>.\n"
"\n"
"<link=\"LUBRICATINGOIL\">Gear Oil</link>: Maintaining efficient operation of bionic systems requires visits to the <link=\"OILCHANGER\">Lubrication Station</link> or use of <link=\"LUBRICATIONSTICK\">Gear Balm</link>. If neither are available, workers slow down to avoid grinding gears.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.PARAGRAPH_2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.PARAGRAPH_2"
msgid ""
"<link=\"BOOSTER\">Boosters</link>: Bionic Duplicants gain specialized building usage and increase attributes by installing boosters. These can be added or removed at any time to customize a Bionic Duplicant's career path or mitigate the consequences of bionic bugs.\n"
"\n"
"<link=\"ROLES\">Skills</link>: Performing colony duties helps Bionic Duplicants earn skill points that can be exchanged for skills that may increase attributes and expand their capacity to install <link=\"BOOSTER\">Boosters</link> and <link=\"ELECTROBANK\">Power Banks</link>.\n"
"\n"
"<link=\"MORALE\">Morale</link>: Morale in excess of a Duplicant's expectations will trigger Overjoyed responses that positively affect a variety of colony functions. <link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSRECBUILDING\">Recreational</link> building usage, <link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSDECORATION\">attractive buildings </link> that increase <link=\"DECOR\">Decor</link>, and improved <link=\"FOOD\">Foods</link> contribute to higher morale.\n"
"\n"
"<link=\"STRESS\">Stress</link>: When Stress levels reach 100%, Bionic Duplicants will exhibit negative Stress responses that can disrupt work and damage buildings.\n"
"\n"
"<link=\"TECH\">Research</link>: Using <link=\"REQUIREMENTCLASSSCIENCEBUILDING\">science buildings</link> unlocks advanced technologies that increase work efficiency and improve the colony's standard of living.\n"
"\n"
"<i>More information about sustaining Bionic Duplicants' well-being is covered in <link=\"MISCELLANEOUSTIPS\">Tips</link> and <link=\"LESSONS\">Tutorials</link>.</i>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Specialized Colony Worker"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONIC.TITLE"
msgid "Bionic Duplicant"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONICBOOSTER.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONICBOOSTER.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"Boosters are programming modules designed to improve and expand Bionic Duplicants' abilities.\n"
"\n"
"Boosters consume a significant amount of processing power during access and implementation. Bionic Duplicants can expand their capacity for booster installation by accumulating skill points.\n"
"\n"
"Boosters can be combined to grant a broader range of skills, as well as to counteract bionic bugs that may exist in their original programming."
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONICBOOSTER.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONICBOOSTER.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Bionic Systems"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BIONICBOOSTER.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BIONICBOOSTER.TITLE"
msgid "Boosters"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLISSBURST.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLISSBURST.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"The Bliss Burst is a succulent in the genus Haworthia and is a hardy plant well-suited for beginner gardeners.\n"
"\n"
"They require little in the way of upkeep, to the point that the most common cause of death for Bliss Bursts is overwatering from over-eager carers."
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLISSBURST.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLISSBURST.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Decorative Plant"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLISSBURST.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLISSBURST.TITLE"
msgid "Bliss Burst"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUE_GRASS.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUE_GRASS.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"The Alveo Vera's fleshy stems are dotted with small apertures featuring bidirectional valves through which <link=\"CARBONDIOXIDE\">Carbon Dioxide</link> is absorbed and sticky oxygenated waste is secreted.\n"
"\n"
"The buildup from this respiration cycle crystallizes into <link=\"OXYROCK\">Oxylite</link> ore.\n"
"\n"
"Horticulturists have long been curious about the protective epithelium that prevents the <link=\"OXYROCK\">Oxylite</link> ore from sublimating while on the plant. Unfortunately, it is too fragile to survive handling, and has thus far proven impossible to study."
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUE_GRASS.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUE_GRASS.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Plant"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUE_GRASS.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUE_GRASS.TITLE"
msgid "Alveo Vera"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"Bluff Briars have formed a symbiotic relationship with a closely related plant strain, the <link=\"PRICKLEFLOWER\">Bristle Blossom</link>.\n"
"\n"
"They tend to thrive in areas where the Bristle Blossom is present, as the berry it produces emits a rare chemical while decaying that the Briar is capable of absorbing to supplement its own pheromone production."
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.BODY.CONTAINER2
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.BODY.CONTAINER2"
msgid ""
"Due to the Bluff Briar's unique pheromonal \"charm\" defense, animals are extremely unlikely to eat it in the wild.\n"
"\n"
"As a result, the Briar's barbs have become ineffectual over time and are unlikely to cause injury, unlike the Bristle Blossom, which possesses barbs that are exceedingly sharp and require careful handling."
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Decorative Plant"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BLUFFBRIAR.TITLE"
msgid "Bluff Briar"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BOGBUCKET.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BOGBUCKET.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"Bog Buckets get their name from their bucket-like flowers and their propensity to grow in swampy, bog-like environments.\n"
"\n"
"The flower secretes a thick, sweet liquid which collects at the bottom of the bucket and can be gathered for consumption.\n"
"\n"
"Though not inherently dangerous, the interior of the Bog Bucket flower is so warm and inviting that it has tempted individuals to climb inside for a nap, only to awake trapped in its sticky sap."
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BOGBUCKET.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BOGBUCKET.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BOGBUCKET.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BOGBUCKET.TITLE"
msgid "Bog Bucket"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BRISTLEBLOSSOM.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BRISTLEBLOSSOM.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"The Bristle Blossom is frequently cultivated for its calorie dense and relatively fast growing Bristle Berries.\n"
"\n"
"Consumption of the berry requires special preparation due to the thick barbs surrounding the edible fruit.\n"
"\n"
"The term \"Bristle Berry\" is, in fact, a misnomer, as it is not a \"berry\" by botanical definition but an aggregate fruit made up of many smaller fruitlets."
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BRISTLEBLOSSOM.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BRISTLEBLOSSOM.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Edible Plant"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BRISTLEBLOSSOM.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BRISTLEBLOSSOM.TITLE"
msgid "Bristle Blossom"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUDDYBUD.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUDDYBUD.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"As a byproduct of photosynthesis, the Buddy Bud naturally secretes a "
"compound that is chemically similar to the neuropeptide created in the human"
" brain after receiving a hug."
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUDDYBUD.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUDDYBUD.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Decorative Plant"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUDDYBUD.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUDDYBUD.TITLE"
msgid "Buddy Bud"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BULBLOOM.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BULBLOOM.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"On a molecular level, it is nearly impossible to distinguish between the Bulbloom's translucent bulbar envelope and high-quality arachnid silk.\n"
"\n"
"This combination of strength and extensibility keep its bright bloom intact in even the strongest currents, making this plant a beacon of hope in dark marine environments."
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BULBLOOM.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BULBLOOM.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Decor Plant"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BULBLOOM.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BULBLOOM.TITLE"
msgid "Bulbloom"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"Mimikas are difficult to categorize. Biologists theorize that the <link=\"BUTTERFLYPLANT\">Mimika Bud</link> engages in this rare variation of reproductive mimicry to improve seed-dispersal and survive the extinction of key species native to its original habitat.\n"
"\n"
"These charming moth-like organisms feature a microscopic cluster of phytoprotein \"brain\" cells and are driven by a singular instinct to tend to their host plants.\n"
"\n"
"Due to a monogenic malfunction, however, this plant-tending behavior benefits all of the flora in its area <i>except</i> its own."
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.SPECIES_SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.SPECIES_SUBTITLE"
msgid "Uncategorized Organism"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.SPECIES_TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.SPECIES_TITLE"
msgid "Mimikas"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.SUBTITLE"
msgid "Critter?"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.TITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLY.TITLE"
msgid "Mimika"
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLYPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLYPLANT.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"Mimika Buds are excellent companion plants that provide a farm with the advantages of beneficial insect presence without the challenges of managing an additional critter population.\n"
"\n"
"Inside each tightly wrapped bud is a highly concentrated pool of enzymes and imaginal discs similar to those found in the Lepidoptera insect family.\n"
"\n"
"Under the right conditions, this unique concoction produces a <link=\"BUTTERFLY\">Mimika</link>, an ephemeral pseudo-insect organism that accelerates growth in neighboring plants before settling into its final seed form.\n"
"\n"
"The sight of a <link=\"BUTTERFLY\">Mimika</link> never fails to fill a gardener with awe."
msgstr ""

#. STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLYPLANT.SUBTITLE
msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.BUTTERFLYPLANT.SUBTITLE"
