msgctxt "STRINGS.CODEX.SEATREE.BODY.CONTAINER1"
msgid ""
"This species of the Laminariales order is composed of vertical stems supported by structural vines. What appear to be leaves are actually <link=\"SEAFAIRYSPECIES\">Kelpoles</link>, aquatic critters that consume aeronutrients present in the Tower Kelp's hollow stalk.\n"
"\n"
"Tower Kelp stalks that fail to attract these natural pressure regulators will collapse before reaching maturation."
